  </div>
  <div class="out"><div class="out-lbl">▶ Output</div>Hello, World! 🌍<br>Python mein welcome hai!</div>
  <div class="box tip"><span class="ico">💡</span><span>Python install karo: <strong>python.org</strong> se download karo ya online: <strong>replit.com</strong> ya <strong>Google Colab</strong> pe code karo — kuch bhi install ki zaroorat nahi!</span></div>
</div>

<!-- S2: VARIABLES -->
<div class="section c-blue" id="s2">
  <div class="sec-head"><div class="sec-num">02</div><div class="sec-title">Variables aur Constants</div><span class="sec-emoji">📦</span></div>
  <div class="card">
    <p>Variable ek <strong>naam diya hua container</strong> hai jisme data store hota hai. Python mein type declare karna nahi padta — yeh <strong>dynamically typed</strong> language hai.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cb">
    <div class="cb-top"><div class="dot dr"></div><div class="dot dy"></div><div class="dot dg"></div><span class="cb-file">variables.py</span></div>
    <pre><span class="cm"># Variable banana (type likhna nahi padta)</span>
naam    = <span class="st">"Sachin"</span>     <span class="cm"># str</span>
umar    = <span class="nm">20</span>           <span class="cm"># int</span>
height  = <span class="nm">5.9</span>          <span class="cm"># float</span>
student = <span class="kw">True</span>         <span class="cm"># bool</span>
nothing = <span class="kw">None</span>         <span class="cm"># NoneType</span>

<span class="cm"># Multiple assignment ek line mein</span>
a, b, c = <span class="nm">10</span>, <span class="nm">20</span>, <span class="nm">30</span>

<span class="cm"># Ek value multiple variables mein</span>
x = y = z = <span class="nm">0</span>

<span class="cm"># Value swap — Python ka magic</span>
a, b = b, a

<span class="cm"># Type dekhna</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="bi">type</span>(naam))      <span class="cm"># &lt;class 'str'&gt;</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="bi">type</span>(umar))      <span class="cm"># &lt;class 'int'&gt;</span>

<span class="cm"># Constants (Python mein sirf convention hai, CAPS mein likhte hain)</span>
PI       = <span class="nm">3.14159</span>
MAX_SIZE = <span class="nm">100</span></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="box warn"><span class="ico">⚠️</span><span><strong>Naming Rules:</strong> Letter ya underscore se shuru ho | Spaces nahi | Case-sensitive | Reserved words nahi (<ic>if, for, class</ic> etc.)</span></div>
</div>

<!-- S3: DATA TYPES -->
<div class="section c-green" id="s3">
  <div class="sec-head"><div class="sec-num">03</div><div class="sec-title">Data Types</div><span class="sec-emoji">🗂️</span></div>
  <div class="card">
    <table class="tbl">
      <tr><th>Type</th><th>Example</th><th>Matlab</th><th>Mutable?</th></tr>
      <tr><td><code>int</code></td><td><code>10, -5, 0</code></td><td>Poore numbers</td><td>❌ No</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>float</code></td><td><code>3.14, -2.5</code></td><td>Decimal numbers</td><td>❌ No</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>complex</code></td><td><code>2+3j</code></td><td>Complex numbers</td><td>❌ No</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>str</code></td><td><code>"Hello"</code></td><td>Text</td><td>❌ No</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>bool</code></td><td><code>True, False</code></td><td>Haan / Na</td><td>❌ No</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>list</code></td><td><code>[1,2,3]</code></td><td>Ordered, changeable</td><td>✅ Yes</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>tuple</code></td><td><code>(1,2,3)</code></td><td>Ordered, fixed</td><td>❌ No</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>dict</code></td><td><code>{"k":"v"}</code></td><td>Key-value pairs</td><td>✅ Yes</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>set</code></td><td><code>{1,2,3}</code></td><td>Unique values</td><td>✅ Yes</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>NoneType</code></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Koi value nahi</td><td>❌ No</td></tr>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="cb">
    <div class="cb-top"><div class="dot dr"></div><div class="dot dy"></div><div class="dot dg"></div><span class="cb-file">type_conversion.py</span></div>
    <pre><span class="cm"># Type Conversion (Type Casting)</span>
<span class="bi">int</span>(<span class="st">"42"</span>)       <span class="cm"># → 42</span>
<span class="bi">float</span>(<span class="st">"3.14"</span>)  <span class="cm"># → 3.14</span>
<span class="bi">str</span>(<span class="nm">100</span>)        <span class="cm"># → "100"</span>
<span class="bi">bool</span>(<span class="nm">0</span>)         <span class="cm"># → False  (0, "", [], None = False)</span>
<span class="bi">bool</span>(<span class="nm">42</span>)        <span class="cm"># → True   (baaki sab True)</span>
<span class="bi">list</span>(<span class="st">"abc"</span>)    <span class="cm"># → ['a', 'b', 'c']</span>
<span class="bi">tuple</span>([<span class="nm">1</span>,<span class="nm">2</span>])   <span class="cm"># → (1, 2)</span>
<span class="bi">set</span>([<span class="nm">1</span>,<span class="nm">1</span>,<span class="nm">2</span>])  <span class="cm"># → {1, 2}  (duplicates hat jaate hain)</span></pre>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- S4: OPERATORS -->
<div class="section c-pink" id="s4">
  <div class="sec-head"><div class="sec-num">04</div><div class="sec-title">Operators</div><span class="sec-emoji">➕</span></div>
  <div class="g2">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-label">Arithmetic</div>
      <table class="tbl">
        <tr><th>Op</th><th>Kaam</th><th>Example</th></tr>
        <tr><td><code>+</code></td><td>Jod</td><td><code>5+3=8</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>-</code></td><td>Ghatao</td><td><code>5-3=2</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>*</code></td><td>Gunah</td><td><code>5*3=15</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/</code></td><td>Bhag (float)</td><td><code>7/2=3.5</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>//</code></td><td>Floor div</td><td><code>7//2=3</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>%</code></td><td>Remainder</td><td><code>7%2=1</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>**</code></td><td>Power</td><td><code>2**8=256</code></td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label">Comparison (Result → bool)</div>
        <table class="tbl">
          <tr><td><code>==</code></td><td>Barabar hai?</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>!=</code></td><td>Alag hai?</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>&gt; &lt;</code></td><td>Bada / Chhota</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>&gt;= &lt;=</code></td><td>Bada ya barabar</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="card-label">Logical</div>
        <table class="tbl">
          <tr><td><code>and</code></td><td>Dono true ho</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>or</code></td><td>Ek true ho</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>not</code></td><td>Ulta karo</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cb">
    <div class="cb-top"><div class="dot dr"></div><div class="dot dy"></div><div class="dot dg"></div><span class="cb-file">operators.py</span></div>
    <pre>x = <span class="nm">15</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(x % <span class="nm">2</span> == <span class="nm">0</span>)                  <span class="cm"># False (odd hai)</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(x > <span class="nm">10</span> <span class="kw">and</span> x < <span class="nm">20</span>)         <span class="cm"># True</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="kw">not</span> (x == <span class="nm">15</span>))              <span class="cm"># False</span>

<span class="cm"># Assignment shortcuts</span>
x += <span class="nm">5</span>   <span class="cm"># x = x + 5  → 20</span>
x -= <span class="nm">3</span>   <span class="cm"># x = x - 3  → 17</span>
x **= <span class="nm">2</span>  <span class="cm"># x = x ** 2 → 289</span>

<span class="cm"># Identity & Membership</span>
a = [<span class="nm">1</span>, <span class="nm">2</span>, <span class="nm">3</span>]
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="nm">2</span> <span class="kw">in</span> a)        <span class="cm"># True</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="nm">5</span> <span class="kw">not in</span> a)   <span class="cm"># True</span>
b = a
<span class="fn">print</span>(a <span class="kw">is</span> b)        <span class="cm"># True (same object)</span></pre>
  </div>
</div>

